 "script": "The new White House press secretary is out after just five days. Katie Zacharia is being removed, CBS News reported Friday, citing two US officials. Trump named her October ninth to replace Karoline Leavitt. But her only briefing lasted fourteen minutes, with questions from three outlets. Then she admitted failing the bar exam, though Trump had called her an attorney. Here's what Trump said next. \"If I were you, I'd reconsider.\" Axios says she's the shortest-serving press secretary in modern history. What should a new press secretary get right first? Tell us below.",
